    "key": "dog.seoContent.title",
    "value": "About These Dog Health Calculators"
  },
  {
    "key": "dog.seoContent.intro",
    "value": "Our dog tools are built on peer-reviewed veterinary standards from AAHA, AAFCO, and WSAVA. Here's what each tool does — and why it matters for your dog's health."
  },
  {
    "key": "dog.seoContent.faq1",
    "value": "What is the most accurate dog age calculator?"
  },
  {
    "key": "dog.seoContent.faq1Answer",
    "value": "Our dog age calculator uses the AAHA 2023 life stage guidelines, which account for breed size differences. Small dogs age slower than large dogs — a 5-year-old Chihuahua is roughly 36 human years, while a 5-year-old Great Dane is about 48."
  },
  {
    "key": "dog.seoContent.faq2",
    "value": "How do I calculate my dog's daily calorie needs?"
  },
  {
    "key": "dog.seoContent.faq2Answer",
    "value": "Our calorie calculator uses the AAFCO Maintenance Energy Requirement (MER) formula: RER × activity multiplier. RER = 70 × (weight in kg)^0.75. The multiplier adjusts for neuter status, activity level, and life stage."
  },
  {
    "key": "dog.seoContent.faq3",
    "value": "Which vaccinations does my dog need?"
  },
  {
    "key": "dog.seoContent.faq3Answer",
    "value": "Core vaccines (required for all dogs) include rabies, DHPP (distemper, hepatitis, parvovirus, parainfluenza). Non-core vaccines like Bordetella and Leptospirosis depend on your region and lifestyle. Our schedule follows WSAVA 2024 guidelines."
  },
  {
    "key": "dog.seoContent.faq4",
    "value": "How long are dogs pregnant?"
  },
  {
    "key": "dog.seoContent.faq4Answer",
    "value": "Dogs are pregnant for approximately 63 days (9 weeks) from ovulation. Our gestation calculator shows the expected due date range and key developmental milestones from implantation through whelping."
  },
